note as CONTROL_diagram_29_delegated_access
  NON-NEGOTIABLE CONTROLS
  - No credential sharing or impersonation.
  - The effective actor and delegating practitioner are both audited.
  - Delegates cannot sign clinical notes or prescriptions unless a separate
    jurisdiction-approved professional role explicitly permits it.
  - Grants expire, can be revoked immediately and are evaluated per purpose.
end note


